The script also checks the allocation against the energy accounts. For each activity, the CO2 emitted by fuel combustion divided by the fossil energy that the energy accounts assign to it gives an implied emission factor, in tonnes of CO2 per terajoule. Implied factors by fuel in the inventory range from 57\.7 for natural gas to 76\.8 for liquid fuels in 2022, so an activity's factor should fall within or near that range. @fig-factors shows the result.

::: {#cell-fig-factors .cell execution_count=7}

::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=7}
![Implied CO2 factor of fuel combustion by activity: CO2 from combustion in the air emissions accounts divided by fossil energy use in the energy accounts, last year (t CO2 per TJ). The band shows the range of implied factors by fuel in the inventory.](index_files/figure-html/fig-factors-output-1.png){#fig-factors width=1032 height=740}
:::
:::


Most activities fall inside the band. Activities outside it point to differences of classification between the energy balance and the inventory, for example for the own use of the energy industries and for electricity autoproducers, which are worth reviewing with ONEM and ANME.

## Indicators and export

Emission intensities divide emissions by output or value added at current prices, in tonnes of CO2 equivalent per million dinars. For households, the denominator is their final consumption expenditure, as the I2A manual suggests [@imf2026i2a]. The script [24_export_aea.py](#script-24) writes the accounts to Excel workbooks in English, French and Arabic, with the long table, the bridge table, the accounts of each year by activity and gas, the emissions by source and activity, and the indicators.

# Results

## Emissions over time and by gas

@fig-gases shows emissions of resident units by gas. They stayed close to 45 million tonnes of CO2 equivalent over the period, with a dip in 2020, when activity and travel fell during the COVID-19 pandemic.

::: {#cell-fig-gases .cell execution_count=8}

::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=8}
![Greenhouse gas emissions of resident units by gas (million tonnes CO2 eq).](index_files/figure-html/fig-gases-output-1.png){#fig-gases width=989 height=498}
:::
:::


## From inventory sectors to the economy

@fig-sankey follows emissions of 2022 from the sectors of the inventory to the sections of the economy that emit them. Fuel combustion spreads over every part of the economy. Industrial processes come almost entirely from manufacturing, mainly cement. Agricultural emissions stay in agriculture, and waste emissions go to the water and waste industry. The residence adjustment adds the emissions of Tunisian carriers abroad to transport.

::: {#cell-fig-sankey .cell execution_count=9}

