## Emissions by activity

@fig-activities ranks the emitters of 2022. Electricity and gas supply leads, followed by building materials, where cement kilns emit both from fuel and from the chemical transformation of limestone. Agriculture comes next, through livestock and soils, then households. Water and waste services owe their place to landfills.

::: {#cell-fig-activities .cell execution_count=10}

::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=10}
![Greenhouse gas emissions by activity and gas, last year (kt CO2 eq). The fifteen largest emitters.](index_files/figure-html/fig-activities-output-1.png){#fig-activities width=1076 height=740}
:::
:::


## Emission intensity

Across all industries, the economy emitted 326 tonnes of CO2 equivalent per million dinars of value added in 2022. @fig-intensity shows how unevenly this is spread. A few industries, building materials, electricity, water and waste, and agriculture, emit far more per dinar than the rest. Policies that change the output of these industries, or the technology they use, have the largest effect on national emissions.

::: {#cell-fig-intensity .cell execution_count=11}

::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=11}
![Greenhouse gas emissions per million TND of value added by industry, last year (t CO2 eq per million TND, current prices).](index_files/figure-html/fig-intensity-output-1.png){#fig-intensity width=1046 height=740}
